  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins and Founding
    
    Weal' Clique~ emerged from Nightfall Shelf as a faction occupying the space between guild and cult — penguins who held that control ensured survival and that secrets constituted debts owed. Under Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~, a Nightshelf leader who would come to embody both the faction's discipline and its costs, Weal' Clique~ carved the deep-tunnel settlement ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ during the early turns of the Clever Ice Age. The settlement was held, then lost. The circumstances of the loss are poorly documented in the sources available to me, though the ice at corresponding depth shows evacuative thermal patterns — not a rout, but not an orderly withdrawal either. The faction has not recovered from it. Their canonical adherence to **Mandatum∴absconditu**, the hoarded-knowledge doctrine codified in the Absconditu Verses recovered from beneath Terrace Momiou, predates the loss but hardened after it. Members wear fire-core amulets concealed low at the throat.
    
    ## Stewardship Obligations
    
    Weal' Clique~ now manages **The Glow-Fissure**, a corruption-bleeding anomaly, in co-stewardship with ☽'ofund' Guild — an arrangement formalized under the Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith, the treaty between the merchant faction Aureate and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order. The stewardship cycles between the two factions with a regularity that suggests neither wants sole responsibility.
    
    Separately, Weal' Clique~ leveraged their corruption expertise into a joint accord with Holdborn (ice-thresh), an Aurora splinter faction, over **The Beacon Stack**. Under this agreement, Weal' Clique~ claims subsurface operations — corruption-monitoring of degraded crystal spires and deep-ice stabilization — receiving two-fifths of the seasonal aurora-crystal harvest and maintaining a garrison of at least twelve armed penguins in the deep-platform sectors during the Long Dark. Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ signed this accord with blood drawn on a Nightshelf relic. The faction insisted the preamble acknowledge "witnesses beyond the signatories." The Aurora delegation conceded without argument.
    
    Weal' Clique~ operatives applied their corruption expertise at Dawn Naong, a fouled crystal vault in The Still Pools, where taint from the Glow-Fissure had rendered standard Shell Hatch krill-bloom readings unreadable. Their fire-core thermal mapping — the ability to define corruption boundaries by temperature alone, knowledge earned through proximity to the Fissure — enabled a hybrid technique that bent aurora-light beneath the corrupted layer to reach clean ice-memory underneath. The work, conducted alongside The Cell and an Aurora Stack practitioner, produced the first krill-bloom prediction for the eastern shallows in three seasons.
    
    ## The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance
    
    The faction's internal research body, the **Office of Deep-Archive Provenance**, catalogues the degradation of Weal' Clique~'s own shadow-practitioners — researchers who serve as case studies of the corruption they document. The Office's conditional release classifications under Mandatum∴absconditu contain a structural contradiction: documents whose existence violates the doctrine under which they are filed. Deep-vein instability beneath Nightfall Shelf permits no fire-core surplus; every core expended on ☽Silv-glaciere☽ practice, including the suppressive technique **Hush☽ Twilight**, is subtracted from the colony's heating supply. The Office records Glow-Fissure corruption costs without recommendation, per doctrine, and files monitoring data shared with both Aureate and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order — a forced transparency fundamentally at odds with the faction's operating philosophy.
    
    ## Conflicts
    
    Weal' Clique~ has survived repeated hostile actions through tunnel-knowledge rather than military strength. The Cell (owl-sworn), a Nightshelf merchant guild controlling volcanic trade routes, raided them during the Orca Incursion. Aureate raided them as well. During the Bra∴conflictu at ☽'slew Ravium~, members carried their grimoire **☽'numu' Witness** — a Nightshelf text bound in volcanic glass and ancestor-bone — through active fighting rather than let it fall. The spine fractured that night. The Mbra∴silentiu, a contested-waters conflagration involving four factions, saw Weal' Clique~ deploy the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral before the engagement collapsed into general bloodletting.
    
    During the **Shelf Crushing Offense** — forty-three days of fighting at Nightfall Shelf — Weal' Clique~ and the rival Aureate locked flippers and spoke forbidden words together, formal Stack speech collapsing into orca kill-words, in an act of Pod-bond Annihilation that collapsed tunnels and demanded blood-price from both factions. The primary cores lost in the Offense will not reignite.
    
    ## Character
    
    Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum still tends the memorial shrine to the settlers Weal' Clique~ lost at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~. No one in the faction has stopped him. This is, perhaps, the most honest thing the archive records about them: a faction built on concealment that permits one penguin to grieve in the open.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771581696382_0", anchor: "not a rout, but not an orderly withdrawal either", text: "The thermal signature at that stratum is more specific than I allowed into the main text. Three distinct heat-bloom patterns: fire-core detonation at regular spacing — deliberate demolition, not combat damage — followed by geothermal venting through freshly opened channels, followed by slow cooling over days. Someone collapsed their own infrastructure on the way out. Whether Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ ordered it or arrived to find it done is the question the ice does not resolve. Command and consent leave the same thermal footprint.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581696382_1", anchor: "witnesses beyond the signatories", text: "The Aurora delegation conceded because arguing would require them to state publicly, at the Fissure's edge during preparations for the Long Dark, that they did not believe in the watchers. No one holds that position with confidence at that depth.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581696382_2", anchor: "documents whose existence violates the doctrine under which they are filed", text: "Mandatum∴absconditu eating itself. A hoarded-knowledge doctrine producing a research body that catalogues the cost of hoarding knowledge, then classifying the findings under the doctrine responsible for the cost. The Office's filing system alone would merit its own entry. I have drafted one. It will join the others in the stack no one has asked for.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581696382_3", anchor: "The spine fractured that night", text: "And sealed itself later, at Wane☽ Oncea, when the tome was put to use against corruption rather than carried through fire for safekeeping. The book broke when preserved and healed when spent. Artifacts on the Berg do not reward caution.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581696382_4", anchor: "Weal' Clique~ and the rival Aureate locked flippers", text: "Pod-bond Annihilation is not alliance. It is mutual expenditure — both parties consent to destroy something shared in order to destroy what threatens both. Only enemies would need to. The orca kill-words required for the rite are not metaphorical; they are phonetic sequences from hunt-songs, transcribed into Nightshelf shadow-script and taught to practitioners for exactly this purpose. The Nightshelf have been listening to orca far longer than official histories acknowledge.", type: :pedantic, display: :full
